From: skyjet18 <57456827+skyjet18@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:27:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 43/49] avformat/hls: don't use byterange when loading
 subtitles or playlist

Some servers don't like requests with byterange and will respond with HTTP 416, so disable byterange requests for playlists and for subtitles

Ported to FFmpeg 9.0.2 from 0016-avformat-hls-don-t-use-byterange-when-loading-subtit.patch.
9.0.2 opens the playlist through open_url() instead of io_open; the
option is set in the same dictionary. The subtitle part is placed after
the extended byte range block of open_input().
---
 libavformat/hls.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
index 234fe9e0..c5c68e44 100644
--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -859,6 +859,9 @@ static int parse_playlist(HLSContext *c, const char *url,
         if (c->http_persistent)
             av_dict_set(&opts, "multiple_requests", "1", 0);
 
+        // don't use byterange when loading playlist - some servers don't like that and return HTTP 416
+        av_dict_set(&opts, "seekable", "0", 0);
+
         ret = open_url(c->ctx, &in, url, &opts, NULL, NULL);
         av_dict_free(&opts);
         if (ret < 0)
@@ -1533,6 +1536,11 @@ static int open_input(HLSContext *c, struct playlist *pls, struct segment *seg,
         av_dict_set_int(&opts, "end_offset", end_offset, 0);
     }
 
+    if (pls->is_subtitle) {
+        // don't try to load subtitles using byterange - some servers will respond with HTTP 416
+        av_dict_set(&opts, "seekable", "0", 0);
+    }
+
     av_log(pls->parent, AV_LOG_VERBOSE, "HLS request for url '%s', offset %"PRId64", playlist %d\n",
            seg->url, seg->url_offset, pls->index);
 
